# clang-tidy for the C++ pack: run by `pnpm cpp:lint` (and the edit hook) over every first-party .cpp, with warnings as errors.
# stacks/cpp/run.mjs forces --warnings-as-errors='*' and the header filter itself, and reads each
# layer's evaluated check list (clang-tidy --list-checks): dropping a check in REQUIRED_TIDY_CHECKS
# (stacks/cpp/sources.mjs), here or in a nested .clang-tidy, fails the lint. A finding is fixed, or
# silenced on its line with `// NOLINT(<check>): <why>` (a bare NOLINT is refused).
#
# Off, and why (one line each; the rest of every group is on):
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: fires on every (from, to) pair; types, not lint, fix that.
# - cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers, readability-magic-numbers: knobs live in config/, and
#   tests are full of literal examples.
# - misc-include-cleaner: wants every transitive std header spelled out; noise at this size.
# - misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes: plain value structs (Note, OutboxEntry) are the point.
# - modernize-use-trailing-return-type: style only.
# - performance-enum-size: an int-sized enum costs nothing at this scale.
# - readability-identifier-length: `id`, `i` read fine.
# cpp/tests/.clang-tidy also turns off readability-function-cognitive-complexity (GoogleTest's
# assertion macros inflate it).
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  cert-err58-cpp,
  concurrency-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  google-explicit-constructor,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  modernize-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  readability-*,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-identifier-length
WarningsAsErrors: "*"
FormatStyle: file
